1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography from Wikitree:
2 CONT Lars Eriksson was a church guardian and farmer (Kyrkvaktare och bonde) at Svarttjärn / Bursiljum 8, Burträsk. In 1669 the farm burned down, and they were exempt from tax for three years for rebuilding. While married to his wife Ra
2 CONC chel, Lars Eriksson had a child with Kerstin Johansdotter, the daughter of sheriff Johan Rusk. In 1673 Lars was sentenced to death for this, but the sentence was stayed as his wife had no means to support their seven small childre
2 CONC n. He also had an affair with his wife's step- or half-sister, Karin Östensdatter. In 1679 his wife is recorded as a destitute soldier's widow with many small children and no help for the labor, and was exempt for paying tax on th
2 CONC e home. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dombok (Judgment Book) Entries for Lars Eriksson (from Agneta Olofsson, quoted by Geni, Wikitree, and Kråken):
2 CONT * Dombok 1673-10-21: Alldenstund County Sheriff (länsman), through his letter of 9 October, the deceased must give a district court to declare that he has arrested a farmer in Svarttjärn or Bursiljum, Lars Eriksson, by the name of
2 CONC  what he is suspected of having had an affair with the Sheriff's wife for a few years, and with a step-sister or half-sister, an unmarried maid Karin Östensdotter, as well now with her wanting to move to Norway ... First he was as
2 CONC ked how old is he? He answered that he was seventeen and twenty, that's 37 years old, had been married now for 16 years, had with his real wife Rågial Östensdotter 7 children in his life, 2 dead, one of which the dangerous fire br
2 CONC oke out 3 years ago. Then it was asked how he came to claim his wife's half-sister Karin Östensdotter [daughter of sheriff Johan Rusk]. He answered the wife was at the sheds, his wife's brother gave him some Brandy ... went to his
2 CONC  mother-in-law's farm, which is next to his, and that only his wife's half-sister was at home..... confessed that she would be pregnant..Karin Östensdotter about 20 years old, born in Siljum.
2 CONT * Dombok 1675-10 Lövånger: Länsman Johan Rusk's daughter Kerstin...gave birth to a child with Lars Erikson in Bursiljum. 1675 Lars Eriksson the man is sentenced to life for his misdeed, but the wife sits in great misery, nothing s
2 CONC o much as no cow but seven small children there of what ... cripples. (Kenneth Mossberg)
2 CONT * Dombok 1675-10-26 Lövånger: Lars Eriksson in Bursiljum sentenced to life in year 1673 but pardoned for life (livet benådad) and punished with running the gauntlet (gatlopp). Lars Eriksson had not only recently left his real bed 
2 CONC and had illicit intercourse (lägersmål och olovlig beblandelse) with his wife's half-sister, but also ...again indulged in such wrongdoing with the sheriff's daughter Kerstin Johansdotter and fathered a child with her... 
2 CONT * Head tax list (Mantalslängd): 1679 wife Rägierd poor soldier's widow with many small children and no work help, owns nothing spared all Interests of the household (Kennet Mossberg).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Eriksson, a soldier (soldat) appears on Mantel. (tax rolls) in Mullberget 2, Burträsk for 1669-1678. After that his widow (Rågiel) appears 1679-1689, and after that his son Lars Eriksson appears 1687 and 1695 (Kråken). So tha
2 CONC t means Lars died about 1678.
2 CONT
2 CONT From a cousin Johan S., he writes me in 2024 about Lars: "His original crime was adultery with his sister-in-law. He was sentenced to death [1673] in the district court and while waiting for the court of appeal's verdict, he was u
2 CONC nder house arrest with an ankle shackle at the sheriff's office/home. During that time, he gets the sheriff's daughter pregnant. [Lars was pardoned 1675 to support his wife and seven small children and made to run the gauntlet (ga
2 CONC tlopp) instead. He was executed in 1679.] So the question is whether it is the first crime that he is pardoned from, or if it is both crimes."
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Eriksson is my ancestor in two ways, through both of his sons Marten Larsson, my straight paternal ancestor, and Lars Larsson. Two of Lars' 4th great-grandchildren, Anders Mårtensson b. 1820 and Elisabet Maria Johansdotter St
2 CONC rid b. 1829, married each other in 1848 and had their son, my great-grandfather Anders Andersson Åstrom, who came to America in 1889. Two other sons, Johan and Nils previously left for America in the early 1880s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry verified with Y-DNA:
2 CONT Y-700 DNA haplogroup: I-Y96980 (from Dan Anderson, FTDNA kit 1016097.
2 CONT From: https://www.geni.com/people/Lars-Eriksson/6000000008450805389
2 CONT "Lars Eriksson DNA verified via at least two sons, belonging to Y-DNA haplogroup
2 CONT I1M253>DF29>Z60>Z73>L1302>Y12318/Y12322."
2 CONT [Note, since the above was written I-Y12322 has since been split to I-Y96980:
2 CONT I1-L1302>...I-M6155>I-FT7755>I-Y12328>I-F64529>I-Y12322>I-Y12321>I-Y96980 ]
2 CONT Y-DNA Sources:
